module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.stage_walks_a_subtree_infer_declines_as_a_where_predicate_set

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }

data stage_walks_a_subtree_infer_declines_as_a_where_predicate_set: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "stage_walks_a_subtree_infer_declines_as_a_where_predicate_set" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "structurally guaranteed, because infer_where_predicate_set_edge and node_inferred_subtree_nodes (consumed by program_partition) both ask the one v2.std.type_binder where_predicate_set_edge, so a partition walker cannot demand facts for a subtree infer declines; the class is decidable and fully modeled, and a new walker that bypasses node_inferred_subtree_nodes is a separate walker, not this invalid state" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a module declaring a where-refinement (`type Pos = Int where positive`) is refused at the partition closure as partition_facts_miss, so the program never reaches member emission. v2.compiler.program_partition partition_closure_entry_for_node demands a facts entry for every node of v2.std.type_binder node_inferred_subtree_nodes, and the facts lookup returns Absent for a node under the where-predicate set. HARM: a legal module is refused by a stage that has no opinion about refinements, and the refusal names a partition fact rather than the declined subtree. Sibling of the declaration-binder-edge case recorded at node_inferred_subtree_nodes.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS (executed 2026-10-21 at origin/main bc21a38d56b7, claim_batch built and run in one remote dispatch, rc=1): src/v2/test/claim/emit/module_member_emission.dag a_where_refinement_emits_its_transparent_alias_on_the_production_route_holds FAILs while a_coproduct_beside_a_function_emits_both_in_source_order_holds and a_record_beside_a_function_emits_as_a_struct_holds PASS. A probe test over the same member_emission_refinement_verdict asserts MemberRefused with reason == ^partition_facts_miss and PASSES at main; with the where-predicate set edge also excluded in node_inferred_subtree_nodes (a scratch mutation, reverted) that probe FAILs, i.e. partition_facts_miss is gone and the refusal is a different, later one. CAVEAT: at main the claim file does not resolve at all under claim_batch, because member_emission_supplied_refinement calls emit_module_member without the tree and declarations arguments that gunbc#14387 added; the reproduction above stubs that one helper in a scratch copy. That second defect is separate and is reported beside this row.",
    "EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY (chain re-derivation, DESIGN.md 6b): v2.compiler.infer infer_where_predicate_set_edge declines the where-predicate set (it is a PARKED frontier whose predicate calls emit inhabitance_undecidable_where_predicate_subject_unmodelled), and the walker contract in v2.std.type_binder node_inferred_subtree_nodes says every stage asking infer for facts walks THE SAME set. The walker excludes the binder, order, match-arm-pattern and bind-key edges but not this one, because infer_where_predicate_set_edge lives in infer, which imports type_binder and so cannot be asked from the walker. The predicate must be homed beside the walker (as declaration_binder_edge was) and both stages ask it. Not an identity-key mismatch and not an unclassified alias: the transparent alias node itself has facts; the miss is under the declined predicate set. calm-badger-500's Edge.declaration work is adjacent only if it moves node_inferred_subtree_nodes or the edge label; the repair touches neither.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (typed loud refusal, partition_facts_miss). CEILING: structurally guaranteed, because infer and every walker ask one predicate, so no stage can demand facts for a subtree infer declines. NEXT TRIGGER: the shared predicate lands in v2.std.type_binder with an enrolled RED (a where-refinement module reaches emission) and the existing a_where_refinement claim as the accepted control; the parked where-clause itself is deleted with refinements (operator ruling 2026-10-02), which also dissolves this row's population. REPAIR STATE (2026-10-21): the predicate now has one home, v2.std.type_binder where_predicate_set_edge; v2.compiler.infer infer_where_predicate_set_edge delegates to it (as infer_declaration_binder_edge does) and node_inferred_subtree_nodes excludes the same edges through it. Executed after the repair (claim_batch, one remote dispatch): a reason probe on member_emission_refinement_verdict no longer reads partition_facts_miss; it reads emit_module_member_record_or_refinement_undecided, a member-level refusal from a DIFFERENT producer (module_member_class does not classify the lowered where-refinement as a refinement). The claim a_where_refinement_emits_its_transparent_alias_on_the_production_route_holds therefore stays RED for that later reason and is NOT claimed green. The supplied-member helper now passes the tree and declarations arguments gunbc#14387 added, so the claim file resolves and a_refinement_with_a_lowered_carrier_emits_a_transparent_alias_holds, the coproduct and the record claims PASS. ENROLLED RED: src/v2/test/claim/emit/module_member_emission.dag a_where_refinement_is_not_refused_for_missing_facts_holds isolates the partition boundary (it accepts any outcome except a refusal with reason partition_facts_miss), so the still-red member classifier cannot mask a regression there. It is RED at baseline (the reason read partition_facts_miss at main bc21a38d56b7) and PASSES after the repair (claim_batch, one remote dispatch, rc=0). It is distinct from the earlier scratch reason probe that located the cause: that probe was a throwaway working-tree test, never committed, and is not evidence for this row.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
